WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.740
For nearly a year now, fans of the Marvel
Cinematic Universe have been trying to puzzle

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.710
out where the story is going in the aftermath
of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:13.720
But now a new special look trailer has arrived
for Avengers: Endgame, the franchise's 22nd

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.890
movie, on the very same morning that tickets
for the movie went on sale.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.750
Barely a minute long, the teaser provides
some of the most thrilling and substantial

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.860
Endgame footage we've seen yet.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.340
Want to know how the trailer might clue us
in to what actually happens in the movie?

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.190
Here's a potentially spoiler-filled look at
all the small details you may have missed

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.900
in the special look trailer for Avengers:
Endgame.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.680
Everyone knows Endgame is revving up for a
rematch between the Avengers and Thanos, a

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.019
grudge match which the new trailer seems to
explicitly show.

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:45.039
But what if that rematch happens sooner than
we think?

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:46.319
It's very likely.

00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:50.949
A mix of rumors and reports indicate that
the marketing for Avengers: Endgame features

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:55.749
footage from only the first 15 or 20 minutes
of the movie, keeping the secrets of its story

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:58.969
held close to the vest until the movie has
rolled out in theaters.

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:04.250
While the "15-to-20 minute" window that's
been reported doesn't seem exactly right,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:09.070
Marvel Studios head Kevin Feige has said in
an interview with MTV News that those reports

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.010
are still "somewhat accurate."

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:15.110
If he's being truthful, it implies that the
trailer footage of the Avengers facing off

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.680
against Thanos again won't come at the end
of the movie, but instead somewhere in the

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.950
first act.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.450
This theory tracks with multiple purported
leaks from the movie that have claimed the

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:29.170
Avengers will team up to fight Thanos in space
somewhere in the beginning of Endgame.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.000
It's possible that the team will even defeat
him in this battle… but in a way that prevents

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.730
the fallen from being revived.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:40.000
If it feels wild to you, consider that Infinity
War kicked off with Hulk fighting Thanos within

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.670
the first five minutes of the film.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.550
So if you think it's unlikely that this movie
will hit the ground running with its plot,

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.480
think again.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.300
These are going to be 3 dense hours.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.671
One of the biggest rumors that's been swirling
about Avengers: Endgame is that it will feature

00:01:53.671 --> 00:01:58.200
a significant jump forward in time, with some
reports claiming the whole movie would be

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.630
set five years after Infinity War.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.620
The trailers have finally given us enough
footage to assume that a time jump will indeed

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.840
occur, but in the middle of the movie, rather
than before it begins.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:13.650
The biggest clue about when the Avengers are
at any given point is the hairstyle of Natasha,

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.379
aka Black Widow.

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:20.629
In Infinity War, she memorably sports a blonde
bob, presumably to work incognito as a member

00:02:20.629 --> 00:02:22.510
of Cap's secret Avengers.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:27.450
The trailers for Endgame have shown the character
with both that same blonde hairdo, but also

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:32.159
a return to her longer red-haired style, similar
to what she wore in previous movies.

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:36.379
In the new trailer, Natasha can be seen with
her Infinity War haircut in the Guardians'

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:41.470
Benatar ship, presumably on the way to fight
Thanos somewhere in space an act which seems

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.840
to be predicted by Bruce Banner's line:

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.430
"If we do this, we'd be going in short-handed."

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.609
That phrasing seems to imply that the Avengers
will take the fight to Thanos where he is…

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:53.840
wherever he is.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.760
At the end of Infinity War, Thanos retired
to a peaceful life on a farm on a planet the

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:01.209
Russo brothers have called Titan II.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.400
The special look trailer seems like it might
show the Avengers encountering him back on

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.180
the first Titan, in the still-smoldering rubble
left behind from their first encounter with

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:09.980
him.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.640
Whatever happens in this fight, it seems like
it won't result in the revival of the people

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.499
Thanos snapped away.

00:03:16.499 --> 00:03:21.290
After the Snap in Infinity War, Thanos' gauntlet
was left smoldering and damaged, potentially

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.099
leaving him vulnerable to attack especially
if the team now has Captain Marvel on their

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:26.820
side.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.040
"I like this one."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.799
If they actually do kill Thanos, then it makes
sense why the Avengers and the world would

00:03:37.799 --> 00:03:42.200
begin to move on with their lives afterward
which is what seems to be happening in the

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:47.319
previously-released Super Bowl teaser, which
showed many shots of an abandoned and neglected

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:48.319
world.

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:52.290
But this status quo would be disrupted by
the return of Scott Lang's Ant-Man, who was

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.809
seen in the second trailer roaming around
a world well after the Snap.

00:03:55.809 --> 00:04:00.199
If Ant-Man approaches the Avengers with his
new knowledge of time travel, it could lead

00:04:00.199 --> 00:04:04.969
the team to reunite for a full victory not
just beating Thanos, but keeping him from

00:04:04.969 --> 00:04:08.340
ever killing the trillions of people he did
in Infinity War.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.200
Apart from all of the time travel, time skip,
rematch shenanigans, the new footage also

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.760
shows a remarkably touching moment between
two characters, the relevance of which may

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.780
have slipped by some viewers.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.230
The first trailer for Endgame saw Tony and
Nebula adrift in space on the now-abandoned

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:28.440
Benatar, and the special look teaser seems
to show the moment the two will arrive back

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:32.870
on Earth, with Tony being embraced by Pepper
Potts and Nebula getting her bearings as she

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.150
lands on Earth for the first time.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:39.400
While Rocket saw Groot fall away into dust
at the end of ​Avengers: Infinity War​,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.400
he has no knowledge whatsoever regarding the
fate of the rest of his team.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.450
For all he knows, when he sees the ​Benatar​
screaming into the Earth's atmosphere for

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:52.100
a landing, it's the rest of his team coming
back ready to pick him up and get out of there.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.940
So imagine his surprise when he sees Nebula,
and only Nebula, instead.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.760
This moment, of these two former enemies offering
each other some comfort, is more than likely

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.810
the moment Rocket realizes that he's lost
everyone to Thanos, and it's probably not

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.740
long before these two outer space outcasts
decide to suit up as Avengers instead.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.900
Fans have known for quite a while that the
production of ​Avengers: Endgame​ involved

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:20.950
the recreation of setpieces from past movies
in the MCU specifically the Battle of New

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:24.980
York​ against Thanos' army of Chitauri that
wrapped up the end of the first ​Avengers​

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:25.820
movie.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:30.420
Leaked set photos are the main culprit for
why so many fans figure Endgame will center

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.880
on time travel.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:35.970
But the latest trailer seems to show some
footage of the Avengers actually working in

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.110
the past.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:41.030
During the special look spot, there's a brief
moment​ that shows Iron Man soaring through

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:45.400
the sky in what appears to be New York City,
with the clip looking like it could have come

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.610
straight out of the first ​Avengers​.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:51.680
If anything, it's certainly a much sunnier
look at the city than the rest of ​Endgame​'s

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.500
marketing​ has shown so far.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:58.060
So is this a shot of future Tony soaring through
past New York, working on some plan to get

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.870
the Space Stone out of the Tesseract before
Loki can even begin the invasion?

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:07.810
It seems possible, and even likely, that this
shot is one of our first looks at the ​Endgame​'s

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:09.820
tour through Marvel movies' past.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.140
With this final movie of Phase Three, the
relationship between Iron Man and Captain

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:17.250
America seems to finally be coming full circle.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.150
Just check out this huge moment:

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.310
"You trust me?"

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.760
"I do."

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:26.850
And that looks like more than just a handshake:
it looks like it could be the moment that

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.200
signifies the official repair of their relationship.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.890
This is something we've been waiting for since
the end of Captain America: Civil War, a handshake

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:36.900
three years in the making.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:41.300
One question that remains is just which Tony
and Steve this is.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.770
If this encounter takes place while the Avengers
are travelling through time, then it's possible

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:51.220
that this meetup is of present Tony and a
past version of Steve, or vice versa.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:55.370
It's hard to tell, but it is interesting to
note that Steve is wearing what looks like

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:59.950
his outfit from ​Infinity War​, but without
the beard, potentially implying that this

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:03.060
is indeed a Cap post-​Infinity War​.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:07.090
If that's the case, then this clip really
does show our heroes making good after all

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:12.020
these years, back on each others' side to
face Thanos' ultimate threat.

